  {
   "id": 34,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1010,
    64
   ],
   "size": [
    440,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 3,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    },
    "text": "## 2. Virtual Camera\nA 4D camera editor over the capture. Click **Open Virtual Camera**.\n\n- Fly with the mouse, **I** adds a key, or pick a preset.\n- Each key has lens and roll. Timeline at the bottom: J / K / L, arrows step frames.\n- Retake transfers camera position, target and roll; editor lens animation and capture-time freezes are not transferred. See docs/EDITOR.md.\n- Shift-click keys to multi-select, **G** moves, **R** rotates.\n- **Import camera path** loads a move from another capture using camera-relative data when available. Review composition after import; see docs/PATH_FORMAT.md.\n\nThe move must start on the real camera (every preset does). Start with a modest arc or push. Large unseen-side moves can change detail.\n\nThe move is saved in the workflow."
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2. Virtual Camera\nA 4D camera editor over the capture. Click **Open Virtual Camera**.\n\n- Fly with the mouse, **I** adds a key, or pick a preset.\n- Each key has lens and roll. Timeline at the bottom: J / K / L, arrows step frames.\n- Retake transfers camera position, target and roll; editor lens animation and capture-time freezes are not transferred. See docs/EDITOR.md.\n- Shift-click keys to multi-select, **G** moves, **R** rotates.\n- **Import camera path** loads a move from another capture using camera-relative data when available. Review composition after import; see docs/PATH_FORMAT.md.\n\nThe move must start on the real camera (every preset does). Start with a modest arc or push. Large unseen-side moves can change detail.\n\nThe move is saved in the workflow."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## 2. Virtual Camera\nA 4D camera editor over the capture. Click **Open Virtual Camera**.\n\n- Fly with the mouse, **I** adds a key, or pick a preset.\n- Each key has lens and roll. Timeline at the bottom: J / K / L, arrows step frames.\n- Retake transfers camera position, target and roll; editor lens animation and capture-time freezes are not transferred. See docs/EDITOR.md.\n- Shift-click keys to multi-select, **G** moves, **R** rotates.\n- **Import camera path** loads a move from another capture using camera-relative data when available. Review composition after import; see docs/PATH_FORMAT.md.\n\nThe move must start on the real camera (every preset does). Start with a modest arc or push. Large unseen-side moves can change detail.\n\nThe move is saved in the workflow."
